Steven Furtick was named BMI Christian songwriter of the year, and wrote three of the 25 most-performed songs, including &#8220;Another One,&#8221; &#8220;Goodbye Yesterday,&#8221; and &#8220;Lion.&#8221;

Capitol CMG Publishing took home publisher of the year, representing 19 of the 25 most-performed songs of the year, including &#8220;Made For More,&#8221; as well as &#8220;Altar,&#8221; &#8220;Grave Robber,&#8221; &#8220;If I Got Jesus,&#8221; &#8220;My God Can,&#8221; &#8220;Somebody Prayed,&#8221; &#8220;Take You At Your Word,&#8221; &#8220;The Truth&#8221; and &#8220;Who Else.&#8221;

2018 BMI Compass Award recipient Elwyn Raymer opened the evening with a prayer, while performances included Belle Frantz performing &#8220;Amazing Grace.&#8221; Steven Curtis Chapman welcomed Drew Parker to the stage for a performance of &#8220;Blame Jesus,&#8221; while Jamie MacDonald closed the evening with a rendition of &#8220;Left It In The River.&#8221;

Other songs celebrated during the evening included &#8220;Altar,&#8221; written by&nbsp;Forrest Frank,&nbsp;Lasanna “Ace” Harris,&nbsp;Steve Rice&nbsp;and&nbsp;Willie Scott Jr.; &#8220;Nothin’ Sweeter,&#8221; written by&nbsp;TobyMac&nbsp;and&nbsp;Jordan Mohilowski; &#8220;Running Back To You,&#8221; written by&nbsp;Seph Schlueter; &#8220;Thank you Jesus for the Blood,&#8221; written by&nbsp;Charity Gayle&nbsp;alongside&nbsp;Steven Musso; and &#8220;Unsung Hero,&#8221; written by&nbsp;Luke Smallbone.

The evening also celebrated 18 first-time award winners, including Leanna Crawford, Frankie Holleman, Zachary Kale, Patrick Mayberry, Steven Musso and Megan Woods.
